    "turn_text": "so you mentioned politics entering the court uh... obviously at this point because politics has become our national religion it seems almost impossible not to i had judge napolitano from fox on a couple weeks ago in the middle of the katange brown jacks in hearing and his position was that basically the senate should confirm a judge that is a you know nominated by the president barring something really off the charts like really really beyond unbelievable in the decision that they made that basically the decision should be left to the president and short of something really catastrophic the person should be confirmed now we watch confirmation hearings and on both sides it's it's all sorts of you know dredging out all kinds of horrible things were made up things in the case of Brett Kavanaugh uh... perhaps in katange brown's case the fact that she couldn't tell you what a woman was maybe that was a catastrophic uh... thing that would have qualified but what's your general position on when the president nominate someone what the process should actually look like",
