    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/5/45336.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 42,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, so I looked at that legislation and went through it with a fine tooth comb and what I found were some significant problems. Number one, we're dealing with rampant inflation in this country. The people in Utah are paying an additional $751 each month, every month for their basic living expenses relative to what they were paying at the beginning of just last year. This is a huge defacto tax increase that disproportionately harms the poor and middle class of my state. And it's entirely foreseeable. It is the natural consequence of excessive federal spending. And so I thought that the Ukraine bill should have been paid for, should have been offset, and I introduced an amendment to that effect that would have done that. Also in that same amendment was language that would have stripped out Title V of that bill. Title V is where the worst spending abuses within the bill could be found. Or we're talking a large amount of money. about 15 billion dollars or so that would have gone to activities in the State Department that are at best tangentially related to Ukraine. And in many instances have been linked by this administration itself to the administration's radical climate change fighting agenda.",
